Subject: [PATCH] Ayaneo Pocket DS: swap the two screens, both staying on

Settings.Global dual_display_swap = 1 (set by the M button of AYAHome, see MKey) makes the
bottom panel the default display while the top panel stays on as the second display. Apps see
the swap and need no setting of their own (DS / 3DS emulators for instance). Only in screen
mode 1 (both screens); the stock "bottom screen only" mode is unchanged.

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/AyaneoDualScreenController.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/AyaneoDualScreenController.java
index ea10bd289..062d58627 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/AyaneoDualScreenController.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/AyaneoDualScreenController.java
@@ -50,6 +50,9 @@ import java.util.List;
  * <li>{@code dual_display_mode} 4: bottom screen only. The bottom panel becomes the default
  *     display and the top panel is turned off.
  * </ul>
+ * {@code dual_display_swap} 1 (not a stock setting, set by the M button of AYAHome through
+ * MKey) swaps the two screens while both stay on: the bottom panel is the default display, the
+ * top panel the second one. It only applies in mode 1.
  * Modes 0 (mirroring) and 2 also exist in the stock framework, but AYAHome never selects them;
  * they are handled as mode 1. The applied values are mirrored into persist.tc.* properties,
  * which the stock framework and AYAHome read back.
@@ -70,6 +73,7 @@ final class AyaneoDualScreenController {
 
     private static final String SETTING_MODE = "dual_display_mode";
     private static final String SETTING_POINTER_MODE = "dual_display_pointer_mode";
+    private static final String SETTING_SWAP = "dual_display_swap";
     private static final String PROP_MODE = "persist.tc.dual_display_mode";
     private static final String PROP_POINTER_MODE = "persist.tc.dual_display_pointer_mode";
 
@@ -93,7 +97,7 @@ final class AyaneoDualScreenController {
          * Called with the display sync root held after a mode change: lays out the logical
